    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2205.03687v3</id>
    <title>One phase problem for two positive harmonic function: below the codimension $1$ threshold</title>
    <updated>2022-05-20T15:47:43Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.03687v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.03687v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>What can be said about the domain $\Om$ in $\bR^n$ for which its Green's function $G(z)$ satisfies $G(z)\asymp \dist (z, \pd\Om)^δ$? What can we say about $\Om$ if the Boundary Harnack Principle holds in the form $u/v=\text{real analytic}$ on the part $E$ of its boundary? Here $u, v$ are positive harmonic functions on $\Om$ vanishing on $E$. Is this part of the boundary also nice?
  We discuss these questions below and give answers in very special cases.</summary>
